  - line: 10
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_title: Arrival in Twilight"
  - line: 11
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_time: Y17,511 M7 D32 or later"
  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_chronology_qualification: M7 D32 remains only the last-supported external-world editorial anchor."
  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "Chapter 053 begins already inside a Void Jump from Chapter 052's void aftermath and supplies no measurable ordinary-world elapsed interval."
  - line: 14
    type: narration
    text: "One moment/the next phrasing, nanosecond processing, minutes/seconds warnings, ten-thousand-year history, between-moments ontology, and compressed travel do not advance the framing calendar."
  - line: 15
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_internal_temporal_condition: Already-active Void Jump followed by immediate materialization and an unstated-duration ash-plain traversal."
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_historical_sub-anchor: None in this scene; the Applicator's approximately 10,000-year stellar estimate describes local history rather than present elapsed time."
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_pov: Geralt-centered third person"
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_location: Void transit, Umbrageous ash plain, and the City of Echoes gate"
  - line: 19
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_participants: Geralt; Oreck; Kyh; coherent Luminaire; active Applicator; Violet; Proto-Dracos; three Solantri gate representatives"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_focus: Arrive on Umbrageous, diagnose its starless environment, observe its inhabitants, and reach the City of Echoes."
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_boundary_evidence: The already-active jump, materialization, ash-plain traversal, and first contact at the city gate form one arrival sequence; entry into the city creates the next location and social reset."
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_continuity: Chapter 053 begins during transit to Umbrageous without staging the departure from Chapter 052's void aftermath."
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "Umbrageous is directly established as a physical starless world containing terrain, atmosphere, mountains, the City of Echoes, Solantri, Proto-Dracos, the Sundered Spine, Old Observatory, catacombs, a Spire, Resonance Pool, and Keeper Lentharis."
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "No SPIRE number is supplied, and the source does not precisely establish whether Umbrageous names only the world, only the Spire, or the combined world/Spire intervention target."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_presentation: Transit, environmental arrival, first observation, and initial local contact"
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_cutscene_purpose: Establish Umbrageous as a starless memory-world and introduce its Solantri and Proto-Draco populations."
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_hidden/unshown_intervals: The departure, jump creation, launch, operator, power source, and exact transit duration are absent; ash-plain travel is compressed and undated."
  - line: 28
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_contradictions: Chapter 053 again surrounds the party with Ghost Spire energy during a Void Jump, but it does not stage the jump's creation or explicitly connect the jump to the Chapter 052 retrieval tether."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh, Luminaire, Pyroclast's node, and the Ghost Spire tether are not identified as the jump's operator or power source."
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "The existing transit-provenance drift remains unresolved."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_chronological_overlap: None established; direct but unstaged transit continuation from Chapter 052's void endpoint."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.geralt_physical_state: Inherited burns, chest pain, and marble-white scars remain unresolved and untreated; no healing interval."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.dragon_mail: Stage 1 remains highest named state; sustained-flight capable, damaged, structurally compromised, unrepaired, and unused here."
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.flight: The Void Jump is not a Dragon Mail flight event; sustained flight remains an established but unused capability."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.anchor_symbiosis: Approximately 80% remains the last explicit value; no change."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.foundational_signature: Permanently consumed; no reuse."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.luminaire: Presently coherent, reconstituted, conversational, distinct from the Applicator, and bonded through Geralt's Anchor."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.applicator: Resumes overt activity through environmental and chronometric reporting without explaining its complete silence in Chapter 052; provenance remains technically unauthenticated."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.zaron: Absent; no state resolution."
  - line: 40
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.oreck: Alive, armorless, cleaver-equipped, burned and untreated; no protection or treatment."
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.kyh: Active navigator; the persistent white U-779 mark and shadow-recoil impairment carry forward but are not mentioned or used."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.vek'tar: Absent; terminal ontology remains unresolved."
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.kaelen_objective: Kaelen remains absent; original recruitment objective displaced and unfulfilled."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_state_ledger.five_mikas: All five remain last-established active from Chapter 051, but only Violet is directly restaged in Chapter 053."
  - line: 45
