  - line: 125
    type: narration
    text: "```"
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "The Void Jump to Umbrageous wasn't a transition."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "It was a dulling."
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "One moment, they were in the hard, clear black of the void, the Ghost Spire's energy crisp around them."
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "The next, everything softened."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "The light, the sound, even the concept of color seemed to leach away into a perpetual, weary twilight."
  - line: 133
    type: narration
    text: "They materialized on a plain of ash."
  - line: 135
    type: narration
    text: "It wasn't the violent, scorched ash of Pyroclast."
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "This was a fine, grey powder that fell in a silent, never-ending drizzle from a starless sky the color of a day-old bruise."
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "The ground was featureless, stretching to a horizon obscured by a mist of its own making."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "The air was cold, still, and carried a scent like old paper and damp stone."
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "“Ambient light source: unknown,” the applicator in Geralt’s head reported, its text subdued. “Chronometric analysis indicates local star absent for approximately 10,000 years."
  - line: 141
    type: narration
    text: "Illumination appears to be residual, reflected from distant cosmic structures."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "Probability of photosynthesis: 0%.”"
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "“Cheerful place,” Oreck grunted, his scales already dusted grey."
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh took a step and froze."
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "He looked down at the ash swirling around his boots, then out at the vast, silent plain."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "His twilight eyes widened."
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "“This ash… it remembers,” he whispered, his voice hushed with a weaver’s awe. “It’s not dead."
  - line: 151
    type: narration
    text: "It’s… recording."
  - line: 152
    type: narration
    text: "I can feel it watching."
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "Every step we take, it’s writing us down.”"
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "He is correct, Violet murmured in Geralt’s mind, her harmonics tinged with unease."
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "This is not soil."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "It is memory given particulate form."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "The entire world is an archive of its own death."
  - line: 160
    type: narration
    text: "Luminaire’s presence was a faint, sorrowful chime. “The Sundering of Light."
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "A cosmic event that stripped this sector of its primary star."
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "The Spire’s dormant protocol was a desperate act of preservation."
  - line: 163
    type: narration
    text: "To exist on borrowed, reflected light for ten millennia… it changes the nature of matter itself.”"
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "In the middle distance, shapes moved."
  - line: 166
    type: narration
    text: "Hulking, bipedal figures with sloping shoulders and thick, scaled hides."
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "Proto-Dracos."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "They moved with a shuffling, deliberate gait, heads down, claws sifting through the ash."
  - line: 169
    type: narration
    text: "As one, they stopped."
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "Dozens of rough-hewn heads turned toward the newcomers."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "For a long, tense moment, there was only the whisper of falling ash."
  - line: 173
    type: narration
    text: "Then, as if on a silent signal, they turned and shambled away, melting into the grey mist without a sound."
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "“They’re afraid,” Oreck observed, his hand resting on his cleaver. “But not of us."
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "Of something else.”"
  - line: 178
    type: narration
    text: "Their destination was clear: a range of jagged, black mountains clawing at the twilight sky—the Sundered Spine."
  - line: 179
    type: narration
    text: "Nestled within their foothills, carved into the living rock, glimmered the City of Echoes."
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "The city was beautiful in a haunting, sepulchral way."
  - line: 182
    type: narration
    text: "Structures weren’t built; they were grown—smooth, flowing formations of a pearlescent material that caught the faint light and fractured it into soft rainbows."
  - line: 183
    type: narration
    text: "Solantri moved through the streets, their skin the same nacreous white as their city, their forms emitting gentle pulses of light that flashed in complex, silent patterns to one another."
  - line: 185
    type: narration
    text: "At the city’s main gate, they were met not by warriors, but by a trio of Solantri whose light-pulses were slow, deliberate, and tinged with a cautious yellow."
  - line: 186
    type: narration
    text: "One stepped forward, and its voice emerged not from a mouth, but from the air around them, a harmonic resonance formed from modulated light."
  - line: 188
    type: narration
    text: "“You carry the resonance of the old networks."
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "You are expected, and also… feared."
  - line: 190
    type: narration
    text: "Enter."
  - line: 191
    type: narration
    text: "The Echo Crown awaits your words.”"

